We refer to recent correspondences.

We note that you are considering shipment of cargo to final destination. However, considering low cargo value (USD 15,083.73)and further costs for re-packing, freight, box fee, and risk of uncollected cargo at destination, we are not sure whether shipment to destination is reasonable and cost effective decision.

In the circumstance, we have discussed with P&I Club and agreed that it would be worth sending further or final notice to the cargo interests on the basis of below sentences and then we should consider further steps (ex. disposal or shipment)

the ocean carrier reiterates that under the terms of the contract of carriage and Article IV rule 2 of the Hague/Hague-Visby rules the carrier's responsibility is excluded in respect of loss and damage to the cargo carried under B/L HJSCZP3F342200 / Container CRSU9359554  which was caused by a collision with another ship;  that therefore the ocean carrier will not compensate cargo interests; that Shippers/receivers should be discussing any compensation matter with their cargo insurers and not the ocean carrier; and that if cargo interests do not wish the 541 salvaged cartons to be transshipped at Singapore and carried to Kuwait then cargo interests must send a formal letter of abandonment so that the cargo can then be disposed of.

